   "html_text": "While Schopenhauer’s influence on the early Nietzsche was crucial, it would be misleading to suggest that it was entirely overriding. Of perhaps equal importance was the influence of the composer and librettist Richard Wagner (1813–1883). Nietzsche knew and was on friendly, even intimate, terms with Wagner during the planning and construction of the Festspielhaus in Bayreuth. During this period (roughly 1869–1876), Nietzsche was profoundly impressed not only with Wagner’s artistic achievements a",
   "md_text": "While Schopenhauer’s influence on the early Nietzsche was crucial, it would be misleading to suggest that it was entirely overriding. Of perhaps equal importance was the influence of the composer and librettist Richard Wagner (1813–1883). Nietzsche knew and was on friendly, even intimate, terms with Wagner during the planning and construction of the Festspielhaus in Bayreuth. During this period (roughly 1869–1876), Nietzsche was profoundly impressed not only with Wagner’s artistic achievements a"
